WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.264
Model-serving telemetry focuses on the online path where users, applications,

00:00:04.264 --> 00:00:06.763
or automated jobs request AI behavior.

00:00:06.763 --> 00:00:11.760
That path needs familiar service signals: latency, throughput, error rates, timeout rates,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.259
queueing, concurrency, retries, and fallback behavior.

00:00:14.259 --> 00:00:19.673
These signals show whether the service is meeting reliability and user experience expectations.

00:00:19.673 --> 00:00:21.755
AI-specific metadata adds necessary context.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:26.752
Teams often need model name, model version, route, deployment environment, request class,

00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:30.500
response size, token counts, safety policy result, cache behavior,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.248
and whether a fallback model or route was used.

00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:38.412
This context helps compare behavior across model rollouts, traffic classes,

00:00:38.412 --> 00:00:41.744
and environments without treating every request as identical.

00:00:41.744 --> 00:00:45.908
Good inference telemetry helps teams locate where time is spent.

00:00:45.908 --> 00:00:51.322
A slow response may come from request admission, queue delay, model execution, retrieval,

00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:54.237
downstream services, network transfer, or response post-processing.

00:00:54.237 --> 00:00:55.486
Without that breakdown,

00:00:55.486 --> 00:01:00.484
teams may tune the wrong layer or blame the model for a

00:01:00.484 --> 00:01:02.566
bottleneck that belongs to storage,

00:01:02.566 --> 00:01:04.648
orchestration, or an external dependency.

00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:06.314
Quality signals require care.

00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:09.229
User feedback, evaluation results, labels, content categories,

00:01:09.229 --> 00:01:14.642
and response metadata can be operationally useful, but they may also be sensitive.

00:01:14.642 --> 00:01:18.807
Operational telemetry should avoid logging raw prompts, secrets, personal data,

00:01:18.807 --> 00:01:22.971
or sensitive outputs unless a deliberate governed process requires it.

00:01:22.971 --> 00:01:27.968
Inference telemetry is strongest when it supports reliability, cost awareness, user experience,

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:31.300
and responsible operations without casually expanding data exposure.
